# eoreader6.1 · kernel · turn 029
# Act: REC+  (Recursion aimed at Figure)   Stance: Making   Site: Lens
#
# REC's second use: the frame itself, actually revised. NOT a claim that
# signal-c-outlier.json's anomaly IS or ISN'T signal — this kernel has no
# mechanism earned yet that could witness such a claim, and asserting one
# now would be exactly the confabulation gap-002 named at the very start:
# speaking without witness. What REC+ can honestly do is revise the FRAME
# to stop being silently blind to the question.
#
# turn-21's frame, revised:
#
#   OLD: "signal, not noise" — one binary, decided by NUL's presence/
#        absence mechanism alone.
#   NEW: "signal, not noise" now names a FAMILY of possible mechanisms,
#        of which absence-recurrence (turn-000 through turn-27, fully
#        earned and witnessed) is the first member. Magnitude-anomaly is
#        named as a second, structurally distinct candidate member — NOT
#        earned, NOT witnessed, explicitly flagged rather than folded
#        silently into "not signal" by the accident of which mechanism
#        happened to be built first.
#
# This is the correct shape of a REC in this kernel's own discipline: it
# does not retroactively change what turn-23/turn-27 witnessed (absence-
# recurrence stays earned exactly as it was), and it does not manufacture
# a witnessed answer for the outlier. It changes what the FRAME'S NAME
# covers, on the record, the same way eoreader6's SEED.md Amendment I
# generalized "sensitivity" from a property of a statistic to a property
# of a (statistic, perturbation) pair once a real counterexample forced
# the distinction — not before one existed.
#
# Earning argument: precondition is turn-28 (a demonstrated limitation).
# Refuted if the revision silently discarded turn-23's earned claim rather
# than extending the frame around it — checked: turn-23's own text is
# unchanged and unsuperseded by this turn.

